                <pb facs="0369" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-25T17:00:00-03:00">December 25, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 25—4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>195. Neither Embassy nor Brazilian authorities know anything of conferences
                    mentioned in first paragraph of Department’s telegram No. 98 December 24, 1 p.m.
                    I am, of course, continuing to urge the prompt initiation of negotiations with
                    representatives of American bondholders.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
